&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="troubleshooting"&gt;Troubleshooting
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="1--502-bad-gateway-error-during-nginx-startup"&gt;1. ⚠️ 502 Bad Gateway Error During Nginx Startup
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;If the application initialization of the upstream backend or frontend containers is not complete when the Nginx container starts, Nginx will fail name resolution or connection establishment and return a &lt;code&gt;502 Bad Gateway&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cause:&lt;/b&gt; While container startup order can be managed via &lt;code&gt;depends_on&lt;/code&gt;, the Docker engine alone does not guarantee readiness at the application layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Resolution:&lt;/b&gt; Configure a dynamic resolver in the Nginx &lt;code&gt;upstream&lt;/code&gt; block, or integrate health check logic to allow proxy traffic only after dependencies are verified as healthy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="2--proxy-pass-mismatch-due-to-trailing-slash-in-uri"&gt;2. ⚠️ Proxy Pass Mismatch Due to Trailing Slash in URI
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;The presence or absence of a trailing slash in the &lt;code&gt;proxy_pass&lt;/code&gt; directive changes the URI path forwarding behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;proxy_pass http://backend/api/;&lt;/code&gt; (with trailing slash): The matched &lt;code&gt;location /api/&lt;/code&gt; portion is replaced, forwarding to &lt;code&gt;http://backend/api/posts&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;proxy_pass http://backend;&lt;/code&gt; (without trailing slash): The original request URI is appended in its entirety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If a misconfiguration results in a &lt;code&gt;404 Not Found&lt;/code&gt; on the backend, verify consistency between the trailing slash in &lt;code&gt;proxy_pass&lt;/code&gt; and the NestJS global prefix configuration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="configuration-notes"&gt;Configuration Notes
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🛠️ &lt;b&gt;Infrastructure Health Verification Criteria:&lt;/b&gt; Rather than merely checking that containers are in the &lt;code&gt;Up&lt;/code&gt; state, define ALB target group health check endpoints and L7 response codes (&lt;code&gt;HTTP 200 OK&lt;/code&gt;) routed through the proxy as monitoring metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🛠️ &lt;b&gt;Least-Privilege Port Publishing Policy:&lt;/b&gt; Restrict host port exposure exclusively to Nginx (the proxy tier) and isolate backend and database containers strictly within the internal bridge network to minimize the attack surface.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>